1
00:00:00,947 --> 00:00:05,350
First launch: A first launch opens setup in the Valet window.

2
00:00:05,350 --> 00:00:12,990
First launch: Step 1: where the Woolworths password comes from. Valet keeps a Keychain copy of a 1Password item.

3
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:16,943
First launch: Step 2: approve the Woolworths adapter: the sites it reaches and what each tool can do.

4
00:00:16,943 --> 00:00:24,595
First launch: The review shows the adapter’s code and permissions before anything runs.

5
00:00:24,595 --> 00:00:28,275
First launch: Step 3: which login to use. Choosing an item asks 1Password.

6
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:35,924
First launch: 1Password asks first: unlock it, then allow Valet.

7
00:00:35,963 --> 00:00:39,658
First launch: Pick the login. It may only be typed into the shop’s sign-in page.

8
00:00:39,658 --> 00:00:45,116
First launch: The shop texts a code at sign-in, so Valet may read that code from Messages.

9
00:00:45,116 --> 00:00:54,253
First launch: Step 4: the store whose prices and pickup times you shop with.

10
00:00:54,253 --> 00:01:01,532
First launch: Step 5: connect Claude. Each app gets its own access, and the setup to copy.

11
00:01:01,532 --> 00:01:05,881
First launch: Valet is set up. It lives in the menu bar from here.

12
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:09,707
Finding your way: Six places in the sidebar. Needs you comes first: anything waiting on you.

13
00:01:09,707 --> 00:01:13,529
Finding your way: Sites: every site Valet can work on, and how each is doing.

14
00:01:13,576 --> 00:01:16,748
A site’s own page: Each site has its own page: what it is doing, and whether it’s healthy.

15
00:01:16,748 --> 00:01:19,515
A site’s own page: Tools: what agents can ask of this site, with what each one is allowed to change.

16
00:01:19,515 --> 00:01:22,252
A site’s own page: Permissions: its login, its codes, and its store, each with its own grant.

17
00:01:22,252 --> 00:01:25,855
A site’s own page: Versions: which adapter version is approved, and any update waiting for review.

18
00:01:25,906 --> 00:01:29,012
Activity: Activity: every call an agent made, newest first.

19
00:01:29,012 --> 00:01:33,938
Activity: Open a call to see each step Valet took on the site, and what it sent back.

20
00:01:33,938 --> 00:01:40,223
Activity: The audit log: a hash-chained record of everything, logins and approvals included.

21
00:01:40,311 --> 00:01:45,367
Search: Search finds any place, site, call or setting: ⌘K.

22
00:01:45,367 --> 00:01:47,485
Search: …and takes you straight there.

23
00:01:47,524 --> 00:01:53,650
Connections, secrets, settings: Connections: the apps and agents that can call Valet, each with its own access.

24
00:01:53,650 --> 00:01:56,792
Connections, secrets, settings: Secrets: where each login comes from. Valet shows which, never the password.

25
00:01:56,792 --> 00:02:02,483
Connections, secrets, settings: Settings: notifications, data kept, updates, and reset.

26
00:02:02,555 --> 00:02:07,136
The menu bar: The menu bar panel: today’s calls, each site, and the stop buttons, without opening the window.

27
00:02:07,216 --> 00:02:11,542
Signing in: When a site needs you to sign in yourself, Valet opens its page under a banner that says why.

28
00:02:11,614 --> 00:02:16,170
Signing in: Needs you shows it too, until it’s done.

29
00:02:16,204 --> 00:02:25,947
Stopping Valet: Pause Valet stops every call at once. Lock down goes further.

30
00:02:25,947 --> 00:02:28,494
Stopping Valet: Locked down: every call is refused, with an answer that says why, until you unlock.

31
00:02:28,494 --> 00:02:31,916
Stopping Valet: Unlock puts it back. Cloud agents removed by Lock down have to be approved again.

32
00:02:32,062 --> 00:02:38,293
Reviewing an update: An adapter update waits for you. Until then, that site’s tools are off.

33
00:02:38,293 --> 00:02:47,970
Reviewing an update: The review compares it with the version you approved, and highlights what changed.

34
00:02:47,970 --> 00:02:55,104
Reviewing an update: Approved. Logins don’t carry over to a new version, so choose it again.

35
00:02:55,104 --> 00:02:57,870
Reviewing an update: The site is back on, at the new version.

36
00:02:57,909 --> 00:03:01,665
Asking first: A tool that can’t be undone asks you first, in a window of its own. (A test build here: no MVP Woolworths tool asks.)

37
00:03:01,707 --> 00:03:07,266
Asking first: The agent is told you declined, and Activity records it.
